<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <Description>Desktop transports that feed an ESC/POS stream into a CrossEscPos.Core printer:
      TCP/IP server, RS-232 serial server, and a USB client. Desktop-only (sockets, System.IO.Ports,
      libusb) — not referenced by the browser app.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\CrossEscPos.Core\CrossEscPos.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Serial-port transport (RS-232 / virtual PTY simulation). -->
    <PackageReference Include="System.IO.Ports" Version="10.0.8" />
    <!-- ESC/POS client library used by the Monitor to exercise the emulator. -->
    <PackageReference Include="ESCPOS_NET" Version="3.0.0" />
    <!-- Direct USB printing (libusb). Needs native libusb-1.0 at runtime. -->
    <PackageReference Include="LibUsbDotNet" Version="3.0.224" />
    <!-- Override ESCPOS_NET's vulnerable transitive SixLabors.ImageSharp 2.1.3. The 2026-10-07
         advisory batch reaches every 2.x and 3.x release (the five findings span >= 1.0.0-beta0001
         through 4.1.1) and 4.1.2 is the only patched version, so the previous 2.1.13 pin no longer
         clears the audit and there is nothing in the 2.x line to move to.

         This project's own code calls no ImageSharp API; the reference exists purely to lift
         ESCPOS_NET's transitive pin. ESCPOS_NET 3.0.0 is the latest release and is built against
         ImageSharp 2.x, where one of its public entry points does break:
         ESCPOS_NET.Emitters.BaseCommandEmitter.PrintImage calls Image.Load<TPixel>(byte[]), which was
         removed after 2.x. Measured against ESCPOS_NET 3.0.0:

             ImageSharp 2.1.13 -> PrintImage works
             ImageSharp 3.1.12 -> PrintImage throws MissingMethodException
             ImageSharp 4.1.2  -> PrintImage throws MissingMethodException (the same one)

         So PrintImage breaks at 3.x, not at 4.x, and CrossEscPos.App has already been resolving
         ImageSharp 3.1.12 through CrossEscPos.Rendering.ImageSharp while referencing ESCPOS_NET — it
         was broken there before this change. Nothing in this repository calls PrintImage or
         ToSingleBitPixelByteArray (which does still work on 4.1.2), so no in-repo behaviour changes.
         What does change is this package's floor: a consumer that pairs CrossEscPos.Transports with
         ESCPOS_NET's own image printing moves from a working 2.1.13 to a broken 4.1.2. Shipping five
         known vulnerabilities that block every consumer's restore is the worse trade. -->
    <PackageReference Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp" Version="4.1.2" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
